# FreeBSD/default/file_access_list - 10/23/2026
#     check_perms' database for FreeBSD: owner, group, the setuid and
#     setgid bits and the nine permission bits each file should have,
#     the level of a difference (A ALERT, F FAIL, W or . WARN) and the
#     ids its owner and group findings take. A 0 is a bit that must be
#     off, a 1 one that is expected, a . one not judged; only a bit on
#     that should be off is reported. The modes are FreeBSD's own, from
#     the base system's mtree (/etc/mtree/BSD.root.dist), passwd(5),
#     crontab(5) and rc(8): system files are root's and group wheel's,
#     the password database's master file and hashed copy (master.passwd,
#     spwd.db) and the host keys only root may read, and nothing rc(8),
#     cron or login reads may be written by anyone but root. A file the
#     system does not have is skipped.
#
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
